# DONE — UI Element Compendium, full build

**Site is live: https://artifacts.clydeford.net**

## What this run accomplished

All 16 steps of PLAN.md, executed subagent-driven: a fresh implementer per
task, a task review after each, fix rounds where needed, then a whole-branch
review on the most capable model.

- 918 entries across 45 categories, seeded from the glossary markdown
- 10 authored examples (button, card, modal, toast, tab-bar, badge,
  text-input, select, accordion, table) with live tweak panels and three
  code formats that are guaranteed to agree — the example *is* the HTML tab,
  rendered
- Command palette (Cmd+K), category browse, tier and example filters
- Open editing with revision history and restore, behind a single
  `requireWrite()` seam
- JSON / markdown / standalone-HTML export, JSON import that genuinely
  restores, nightly R2 backup keeping 30 copies
- 209 unit tests, 11 Playwright acceptance tests covering all eight checks in
  section 12 of the source spec
- Zero runtime dependencies; no build step

## Left unfinished / needs attention

1. **The first R2 backup object is unverified.** The cron `0 3 * * *` is
   registered and was double-confirmed via the Cloudflare API, but it had not
   fired when the run ended. **Check that `backups/2026-08-19.json` exists in
   the `compendium-backups` bucket.** If it does not, the durability story is
   incomplete and nothing else in the build will tell you.

2. **908 of 918 entries are definition-only.** That is by design — the plan
   authored 10 to prove the tweak system — but the site will look sparse until
   more are written. The Edit view and the "definition only" filter exist for
   exactly this.

3. **Editing is open with no login, deliberately.** `EDIT_KEY` is unset, so
   `requireWrite()` returns null and anyone can edit, import or re-seed. The
   revision history and nightly backup are the mitigations. Setting `EDIT_KEY`
   as a Worker secret locks every write route with no other code change —
   that seam was tested.

4. **Deferred, judged fine to leave** (detail in the ledger): `listRevisions`
   has no pagination; the test helper splits SQL naively on `;`; markdown
   export collapses newlines in a definition (JSON is the lossless format);
   the plate's per-category lean uses a `data-lean` attribute rather than the
   `--plate-lean` custom property the spec described.

