## Recommended starting point for the next run

**Verify the backup fired**, then author examples for the next tranche of
core-tier entries. The tweak system is proven end to end, so authoring is now
content work rather than engineering: each entry needs a `controls_schema` and
three templates, and `tests/examples.test.js` mechanically enforces that every
control is referenced by every format and that no template emits a warning.

Before that, one decision worth taking deliberately: whether to set `EDIT_KEY`.
The site is currently world-editable, which was your explicit choice, but it is
worth re-confirming now that it is actually public rather than hypothetical.

